//! Golden differential tests against the Go implementation (fixtures generated by
//! `go run -mod=vendor ./hack/golden/ovshugepages crates/ctrl-ovshugepages/tests/fixtures`).
//!
//! Each `<scenario>.json` fixture holds the scenario's inputs (pull secret variant, whether the
//! hosted client is injected, fake ReleaseImageReader answers, seed Namespaces, and per step:
//! size/amount/release, an injected BadRequest failure for a verb/resource, external edits of
//! the Namespace/DaemonSet, re-injection of the hosted client) and the Go outputs per step.
//! The Rust [`Manager`] is driven with the same inputs against `ctrlrt-fake` (management
//! cluster) and a client-go-semantics fake clientset (hosted cluster) and must produce, byte
//! for byte: the error string, whether the hosted client is still cached, the reader calls,
//! the log records (`V<level> <name>: <msg> <json kvs>`) and the `encoding/json` bytes of the
//! hosted Namespace and DaemonSet after each step.
//!
//! Normalization: none on the Rust side. The Go generator talks to its fake clientset through
//! a real `*kubernetes.Clientset` over an in-process HTTP transport; it stores request bodies
//! with an empty TypeMeta (as a direct typed fake call would) and drops client-go's own
//! REST tracing log records (V > 4). Where Go panics (`resource.MustParse` on an invalid
//! size) the fixture records the panic message with `panic: true`; the Rust port returns that
//! message as an error instead.
//!
//! `Namespace`/`DaemonSet` are k8s-openapi types whose serde field order and empty-value
//! handling differ from Go's; [`go_namespace`]/[`go_daemon_set`] encode them in Go field order
//! with Go `omitempty` rules (metadata via `apis::go`), and [`assert_lossless`] checks that the
//! mirror dropped no data.

